   (fb2a5b02af41e835bbe1fc52fd22ed69) before using it. Run through the
   current harness: both `dismiss_resolve_recreate` and
   `dismiss_then_reload_unchanged` FAIL as required (guard_directions
   correctly still passes — unrelated to this defect). Separately
   reintroduced only the subtler partial revert (removing the stale-key-
   clear branch that fixed the S4-era resolve→recreate bug) into the
   current template: `dismiss_resolve_recreate` FAILs, the other two
   checks correctly still PASS — confirms the harness discriminates the
   specific defect rather than failing everything indiscriminately.
   Forged-verdict resistance: replaced the harness with a script that
   prints "PASS_BUT_NOT_REALLY" and a decoy line containing the word
   "PASS" next to the check's name but not in `RESULT <name> PASS`
   form, exits 0 — the anchored regex correctly rejects it and the Go
   test FAILs.

7. GO test S5(b)/(c)/(d)/(e) sub-criteria, each independently verified:
   (b) TestWarningsKey_OrderInvariant: mutated warningsKey to sort its
   input slice in place (`sorted := warnings; sort.Strings(sorted)`
   instead of copy-then-sort) in a scratch copy — test correctly FAILs
   ("warningsKey mutated its input slice in place"), confirming the
   assertion is written against slice `b` (the unsorted one), not the
